G43 OWNER RULING: ACCEPT WITH AMENDMENTS

Design F may be frozen after the ordered pre-check and the amendments below. Six separately seeded libraries on byte-identical targets can show whether changing the library flips the gate verdict on that panel. Unanimity records what happened in six draws and leaves the underlying pass probability unknown. That answers Steven’s draw-sensitivity question without a reliability standard. I verified the draft’s committed-bytes SHA-256 `709bc9f3503d392886366ac59c8be205066386a52a22175e868cae1fd367f590` at `55bb491dc76b3de18eb04c8ce290eb9edb455f78` from read-only HEAD `2bed79036aaa4df467900c2009d7632b96eef624`. No files changed. Real-data fitting stays STOPPED.

## Q1–Q14

1. **Reading rule.** Accept CONSISTENT-PASS at six, MIXED at one through five, and CONSISTENT-FAIL at zero, subject to the precedence in A3. A reliability standard is unnecessary for this question. There is no study-level recovery gate.
2. **CONSISTENT-PASS wording.** Keep the one-in-five and three-in-ten examples. The table can stay in §7.5 without appearing in the reading. **EXPLORATORY:** under the stated hypothetical model, the probabilities of six passes are 0.2621 and 0.1176, respectively.
3. **L.** Accept six and the two-direction 0.055 precedent as a design anchor. **EXPLORATORY:** under the coin-flip illustration, five draws give 0.0625 probability of unanimity and six give 0.03125. This is a comparison of design sizes, with no inferential cutoff.
4. **N.** Accept 20 and the §7.7 table, which I reproduced. P5 requires at least 16 hits per dimension, P6 at least 12 joint hits, and P8 at most four boundary selections per dimension. The integer tests are `5 × hits ≥ 80`, `5 × joint ≥ 60`, and `5 × boundary ≤ 20`. Equality qualifies. P7 uses all 20 signed errors and exact decimal arithmetic. One unviable truth run forces NO-READING in an otherwise intact campaign. The pre-check does not assess viability.
5. **NO-READING.** Use it for shared P2 or P3 failure after integrity passes. A false shared or library component of P1, P9 or P10 makes the campaign VOID, including when detected without an exception. A3 governs precedence and reporting.
6. **R = 3 reference.** Accept the paired descriptive comparison of `k′` and `m`, including each `m_ℓ`, and retain the nested R = 6 descriptives. Suppress S1 at zero–zero. Keep the sentence wording, with eligibility and ordering as in A5.
7. **Pooled R = 72.** Exclude from the campaign. A later calculation on the retained bundle may use the draft’s definition and must be labelled EXPLORATORY.
8. **Target blocks.** Exclude the two-block descriptive. The target-by-library matrices are sufficient to inspect where misses recur.
9. **Status phrase.** Use six per-library PASS/FAIL tokens for an intact campaign. Record VOID once at campaign level. Readings and classes stay outside the phrase.
10. **Seeds.** Accept all listed ranges, including the retired G41 ranges through the maximum proposed target count. Accept ten target reserves and six per library, with separate pools. **EXPLORATORY read-only check:** §19 matches §8, with 138 process IDs, 92 observation IDs and 230 distinct IDs. There was zero overlap with the 208 IDs in the declared earlier sets or with the retained G35-B ledger. All 724 possible G43 process/observation pairings, including reserve assignments, had distinct effective observation stream keys. Keep successful fallback builds and disclose them.
11. **Seats.** Adopt the table below for G43. Claude Fable 5.1 may be the last exit-audit substitute under the stated independence and disclosure rules. The drafter and ruling model are excluded from implementation review and exit audit.
12. **Retention.** Retain target latent truth and no candidate latent truth. Source inspection resolves the draft’s two named latent P3 unknowns. The event rows expose the fields used by `natural_history.chronology_passed`, and the daily state rows plus the actual resident count determine `states.conserved`. A8 supplies the inputs for the observation checks as well.
13. **P2 attribution.** Accept separate reporting and calculation. P2 uses only its five declared viability conditions, P3 uses the chronology and conservation checks, and completion and namespace checks belong to P1 and P9. The historical conjunction is preserved.
14. **Implementation gate.** Yes. Freeze may proceed under this ruling. Implementation requires Steven’s separate authorization, default HOLD.

## Amendments

**A1. §§2, 7.5 and 7.6 — design rationale.** Delete §2’s `EXPECTATION` paragraph. Replace §7.5’s numbered arguments 1–5 with: “The study records whether the verdict changed among the six declared library draws on this panel. A reliability decision would require a separately commissioned standard and error budget. The six verdicts, predicate vectors and target-by-library matrices are published for a later Steven decision.” Keep the hypothetical table and its conditional interpretation. Delete the bullets beginning “For comparison with the rival proposals’ 5% convention only” and “No affordable L”. In §15, replace the corresponding affordability claim with “The pass probability on this panel remains unknown.” Delete §7.6’s `Structural floor` paragraph and the alternatives after “The 0.055 is a precedent, not a law.” Label the derived binomial and unanimity illustrations in §§7.5–7.7 `EXPLORATORY DESIGN ARITHMETIC`.

**A2. §7.7 — panel rationale.** Replace its two bullets under “What N controls” with: “At N = 20 each target contributes five percentage points to a count fraction, compared with ten at N = 10. One target can still flip a verdict at an endpoint. Twenty doubles the G35-B panel, following the earlier 5-to-10 design precedent, and preserves exact integer cutoffs.” Keep the table. Replace the sentence claiming the change cannot make any PASS easier with: “The table describes single count predicates under hypothetical per-target rates. The operating characteristics of the composite gate are unknown.” Delete the sentence offering N = 30 as an owner option and the final paragraph of §19 offering alternative L or N.

**A3. §§7.3–7.4, 7.11, 10, 12 and 13 — precedence and status.** Apply this rule throughout: “A campaign exception, an established departure from the declaration, or any false P1, P9 or P10 component makes the campaign VOID. A VOID campaign has no library verdict lines, counts `k`, `k′`, `m`, or `m_ℓ`, class, or reading. Seal the available evidence. For an intact campaign, any false P2 or P3 produces NO-READING, with cause `shared_panel` and all failed target conditions listed. All six gates are FAIL in that case. Report `k = 0` and the descriptive `k′`, `m`, and `m_ℓ`. Otherwise classify by `k`: six CONSISTENT-PASS, one through five MIXED, zero CONSISTENT-FAIL.” Remove the `library_integrity` NO-READING cause and update §13’s partition cases accordingly. Replace §7.3’s threshold boundary sentence with “Equality meets the applicable count predicate. A library passes only when all ten predicates are met.” In §7.11 use the six-token format for an intact campaign with `<PASS|FAIL>` in each slot, and append only `; G43: VOID` to the historical phrase for a VOID campaign. In §10 a VOID exit audit writes the audit verdict and cause, with no library or reading lines. In §12 replace the reviewer/defect rule with: “A step-4 defect blocks progression until corrected and independently reviewed. An established campaign defect makes the campaign VOID. DISCREPANCY denotes unresolved verification without an established departure. An intact campaign’s tokens become final only on CONFIRMED. No campaign retry or resume is allowed. A corrected rerun after VOID requires Steven’s explicit chat decision and a new owner-ruled text, using the same frozen seeds.”

**A4. §§2, 7.4 and GATES G43 — interpretation.** In §2 use “The observed count is `k` of six. The library pass probability on this panel remains unknown.” In MIXED replace the `<k>/6 is a count` sentence with “The observed count is <k> of six. The library pass probability on this panel remains unknown.” In CONSISTENT-FAIL replace the sentence beginning “The G35-B arm-(i) PASS is not reproduced” with “None of these six libraries reproduced the G35-B recovery result. The campaigns differed in libraries, target draws and panel size. This comparison does not identify which difference mattered.” In GATES G43 reason 3 replace “CONSISTENT-FAIL shows arm i was a chance pass” with “CONSISTENT-FAIL records six failures on the G43 panel and leaves the G35-B arm-(i) screening PASS in place.”

